Hello! I'm a software engineer and I write here about free and open source
software, politics, ethics, and philosophy. I'm the founder & maintainer of
several open source projects, notably [SourceHut], the [Hare programming
language], and [Vim Classic], and I started but no longer work on several more
that you might have heard of, such as [sway], [wlroots], [aerc], and many
others.

[SourceHut]: https://sourcehut.org
[Hare programming language]: https://harelang.org
[Vim Classic]: https://vim-classic.org
[Sway]: https://swaywm.org
[wlroots]: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/wlroots/wlroots
[aerc]: https://aerc-mail.org

I like getting emails so if you have comments or feedback on anything you read
here, feel free to [reach out directly] or to write to my [public inbox]. It
might take me several days to get to your email.

The content for this site is [CC-BY-SA] and the [source code] is [MIT]. The
theme is based on [The Proportional Web] by Oskar Wickström, modified to suit my
personal preferences and the needs of this blog. Wickström's work uses the MIT
license.

[The Proportional Web]: https://owickstrom.github.io/the-proportional-web/

**I do not use** large language models (LLMs) or other forms of generative AI,
including anything on this website and all of my software projects.

[public inbox]: https://lists.sr.ht/~sircmpwn/public-inbox
[reach out directly]: mailto:drew@ddevault.org
[CC-BY-SA]: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0/
[source code]: https://git.sr.ht/~sircmpwn/drewdevault.com
